# CODEOWNERS — review ownership for the protected real-time audio boundary.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE DOES AND DOES NOT DO
#
# GitHub uses this file to request review from the listed owners automatically.
# It only *blocks* a merge when the branch protection rule for the target branch
# has "Require review from Code Owners" enabled. Without that setting this file
# is an advisory reviewer-suggestion list and nothing more.
# See docs/realtime_audio_branch_protection.md for the exact settings required
# and their current status.
#
# A WARNING ABOUT NONEXISTENT OWNERS
#
# If a pattern lists a user or team that does not exist, or that lacks write
# access to this repository, GitHub does not error — it silently assigns no
# owner, and the rule fails open. That is the worst outcome for a protection
# file, so every handle below is one evidenced from this repository's own
# configuration. Do not add a team handle here before creating the team.
#
# Evidenced owner: `git remote -v` resolves to
# git@github.com:hmcroody-alt/CoinPilotX.git, so @hmcroody-alt is the account
# that owns this repository.
#
# TODO(repository administration): if real-time audio should be owned by more
# than one person, create a team (suggested: @hmcroody-alt/realtime-audio-owners)
# and replace @hmcroody-alt on the audio blocks below. Do not add the team handle
# until the team exists and has write access.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default owner for everything, so no path is unowned.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                                                       @hmcroody-alt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The lock itself. Changing the manifest, the gate, the workflow, or this file
# changes what is enforced everywhere else, so it is owned first.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/config/realtime-audio-protected-paths.json             @hmcroody-alt
/scripts/realtime_audio_change_gate.py                  @hmcroody-alt
/.github/workflows/realtime-audio.yml                   @hmcroody-alt
/.github/CODEOWNERS                                     @hmcroody-alt

